  "Number": 32,
  "Question": "Let a sequence \\(\\{u_n\\}\\) be defined by \\(u_1=5\\) and the relation \\(u_{n+1}-u_n=3+4(n-1),\\) \\(n=1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(\\ldots.\\) If \\(u_n\\) is expressed as a polynomial in \\(n,\\) the algebraic sum of its coefficients is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Setting a polynomial's variable equal to \\(1\\) turns each term into its coefficient, including its sign. If the polynomial representing \\(u_n\\) is\n\\[\nF(n)=c_0+c_1n+\\cdots+c_kn^k,\n\\]\nthen\n\\[\nc_0+c_1+\\cdots+c_k=F(1).\n\\]\nHere \\(F(1)=u_1=5\\). Therefore the algebraic sum of the coefficients is \\(\\boxed{5}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
